# Viewrr — EAS build upload context.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# Only `eas-cli` reads this file. Git, Vite, Render, Node, npm and the Viewrr
# web/server build all ignore it completely — it is not a .gitignore and it
# changes nothing about what the repository tracks or what Render deploys.
#
# WHY IT LIVES AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT AND NOT IN mobile/
# Before every build, `eas-cli` compresses an "archive root" and uploads it. It
# resolves that root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, so the archive root is
# this whole repository, and `.easignore` is only read from that same root. A
# file at mobile/.easignore is never read and would have no effect.
#
# WHAT IT FIXES
# Without this file the upload was ~339 MB, measured as:
#   ~205 MB  the shallow clone's .git (this repo tracks ~22.7k files under the
#            root node_modules/, plus the marketing videos, so the packfile is huge)
#   ~138 MB  client/ — the web marketing site, of which client/public/videos is 137 MB
#    ~0.9 MB mobile/ — the app EAS is actually building
# The iOS/Android app needs none of the web app, so none of it is uploaded.
#
# VCS INTEGRATION IS UNAFFECTED
# `.git` below only removes git metadata from the uploaded tarball. `eas-cli`
# still runs as a normal Git-aware build: it reads the commit hash and message
# from this working repository, so the EAS dashboard keeps full build/commit
# traceability. EAS_NO_VCS is deliberately NOT used.
#
# IMPORTANT CAVEAT WHEN EDITING
# As soon as this file exists, `eas-cli` STOPS reading every .gitignore in the
# repository, including mobile/.gitignore. Every rule the upload needs must
# therefore be restated here.
#
# NEVER EXCLUDE — the mobile build depends on all of these:
#   mobile/src/  mobile/assets/  mobile/app.config.ts  mobile/eas.json
#   mobile/package.json  mobile/package-lock.json  mobile/tsconfig.json
#   mobile/.env.example
# mobile/ is a fully isolated package (its own package.json, lockfile, Expo and
# TypeScript config, no npm workspaces), which is what makes this safe.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git metadata and installed dependencies.
# EAS reinstalls dependencies on the build worker from mobile/package-lock.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
node_modules

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Viewrr web app and backend. Not inputs to the React Native build.
# Nothing is deleted from the repository — these are simply not uploaded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/client/
/server/
/shared/
/migrations/
/script/
/attached_assets/
/dist/
/drizzle.config.ts
/components.json
/postcss.config.js
/tailwind.config.ts
/vite.config.ts
/render.yaml
/*.md

# Root package.json, package-lock.json and tsconfig.json are intentionally KEPT.
# They are a few hundred KB and eas-cli inspects the archive root when working
# out whether the project sits inside a monorepo, so their presence matches the
# layout of every build made so far.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated native projects. Managed (CNG) workflow — EAS runs `expo prebuild`
# on the worker, so any local ios/ or android/ folder is stale.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mobile/ios/
mobile/android/
mobile/.kotlin/
*.orig.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expo, Metro and TypeScript caches and build output — all regenerated.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mobile/.expo/
mobile/dist/
mobile/web-build/
mobile/expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local, machine-specific environment files and databases.
# The EAS build reads APP_ENV from the matching eas.json build profile, so no
# .env is needed in the archive. mobile/.env.example is deliberately kept.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signing material. EAS uses the credentials stored in the Expo project;
# nothing signing-related should ever travel inside an upload.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and test artefacts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
shots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS cruft.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Developer tooling the native build never runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mobile/scripts/
